cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or refer to this work, please cite it as below."
title: "CNM-BERT: A Drop-In Structural Embedding for Chinese Characters via Ideographic Description Sequences"
abstract: >-
  Token-based encoders like BERT treat Chinese characters as atomic identifiers,
  ignoring their recursive orthographic structure. The Compositional Network Model
  (CNM) is a lightweight, drop-in augmentation that parses Ideographic Description
  Sequences into trees, encodes them with a recursive Tree-MLP, and fuses the
  resulting structural embeddings into BERT without modifying the backbone.
type: software
